PU300420-7844562	30/04/2020	Partial relief Granted	"Subject: Sajjad and ISRAR UI HAQ(03156917269) Illegally disconnect the meter of Sui gas Dated on 30-04-2020 :: The employes  of Sui northern gas pipe lines limited Mr rafaqat Mr sajjad  and ISRAR ul haq Illegally disconnect our meter of Sui gas and misuse of their powers and insulted our family.there are no arrears whatsoever pending according to the billing history provided for in the bill issued by the company and the furthermore, there is also no mention of tempering or faulty meter as far as the meter of us, /consumer is concerned. We produced before the employs of company original bill for the month of March 2020 amounting to Rs. 1790 which has been duly paid to the company. Therefore according to section 29 of the gas (theft, control and recovery) Act, 2016,the gas company not to Illegally disconnect the Sui gas meter of consumer. Therefore I requested that the employes of gas company misused their powers and Illegally worried us.. So plz must take action against gas company and employes and restore the connection of our Sui gas meter. Our family members are worried about that. Thanks."	"Dear Citizen,
We wish to inform that on 16.03.2020 disconnection of your Sui gas connection (removal of regulator) was done due to non-payment of bill by the billing section (snap shot of disconnection attached). After a few days of removal of regulator you installed regulator and started using gas illegally (pictorial evidence attached). Our team visited your premises three times and advised you to remove the illegal regulator and visit Sui gas office and get your reconnection processed but you did not comply with the instructions given by SNGPL officials, therefore your meter #CT189833054 bearing consumer #52604700006 was removed on 30.04.2020, you are once again advised to visit Sui gas office with required documents and get your reconnection processed. 
We will continue to serve you to the best of our abilities.
